{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463392",
      "title": "Vue App Lifecycle - Theory",
      "lectureOrder": 68,
      "videoOrder": 61,
      "sourceHash": "5f93ce3c5cfc287b39891a69d58c18cb6a9dea8c28acfe8d738e13be09ddd3e8",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 1.493,
          "end": 4.55,
          "en": "Now to concludes this module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.55,
          "end": 9.08,
          "en": "we'll have our second lecture, which you should not skip.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.08,
          "end": 11.04,
          "en": "The first one was the refs lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.04,
          "end": 14.57,
          "en": "Now we're going to talk about the Vue Instance Lifecycle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.57,
          "end": 16.46,
          "en": "which is also important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.46,
          "end": 18.51,
          "en": "We learned how Vue works under the hood,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.51,
          "end": 20.28,
          "en": "we learned about the virtual DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.28,
          "end": 22.2,
          "en": "and that there are various steps",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.2,
          "end": 24.82,
          "en": "for bringing something onto the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 24.82,
          "end": 28.94,
          "en": "Sometimes you need to run code during those steps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.94,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "And that's why Vue has a quite elaborate life cycle,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 34.98,
          "en": "where you can step in at any time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.98,
          "end": 37.46,
          "en": "to execute code you need to execute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 37.46,
          "end": 40.13,
          "en": "And you will see some of those lifecycle hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.13,
          "end": 42.58,
          "en": "we're going to discuss now in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 42.58,
          "end": 44.65,
          "en": "throughout this course, by the way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 44.65,
          "end": 46.98,
          "en": "It all starts with us creating a new app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.98,
          "end": 50.3,
          "en": "And of course, mounting it with the mount method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.3,
          "end": 52.43,
          "en": "to the HTML code, to the DOM,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 52.43,
          "end": 55.87,
          "en": "so that Vue knows where to render the app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.87,
          "end": 58.44,
          "en": "Then, when it starts creating the app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 58.44,
          "end": 60.96,
          "en": "and starts bringing something on to the screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 60.96,
          "end": 65.96,
          "en": "it reaches a couple of points, a couple of lifecycle phases,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.22,
          "end": 70.76,
          "en": "which are also reflected in methods",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.76,
          "end": 74.5,
          "en": "you can add to your Vue app configuration object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.5,
          "end": 78.41,
          "en": "to run code you might need to run at this point of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.41,
          "end": 81.19,
          "en": "For example, the first lifecycle phase,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 81.19,
          "end": 83.303,
          "en": "the first so called lifecycle hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.303,
          "end": 87.6,
          "en": "that is reached is the beforeCreate phase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.6,
          "end": 89.89,
          "en": "It's followed by a created phase.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.89,
          "end": 92.14,
          "en": "The difference is that beforeCreate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 92.14,
          "end": 94.88,
          "en": "is basically called before the app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 94.88,
          "end": 96.95,
          "en": "has been fully initialized,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 96.95,
          "end": 99.63,
          "en": "whereas created is called thereafter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 99.63,
          "end": 101.21000000000001,
          "en": "At this point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 101.21000000000001,
          "end": 103.6,
          "en": "we still have nothing on the screen though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 103.6,
          "end": 107.91,
          "en": "After created Vue just knows its data properties,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 107.91,
          "end": 111.163,
          "en": "and it's aware of the general app configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 112.53999999999999,
          "end": 116.503,
          "en": "But now's the time where the template is compiled.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.39,
          "end": 120.03,
          "en": "So where all the dynamic placeholders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 120.03,
          "end": 123.28,
          "en": "all the interpolations and so on are removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.28,
          "end": 125.57,
          "en": "and replaced with the concrete values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 125.57,
          "end": 127.253,
          "en": "that should be shown to the user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.187,
          "end": 132.62,
          "en": "Thereafter the before mount hook is reached",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.62,
          "end": 136.25,
          "en": "Before mount means that this is right before Vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.25,
          "end": 139.76,
          "en": "is actually going to bring something to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.76,
          "end": 143.233,
          "en": "So right before we can see something on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.17000000000002,
          "end": 148.41,
          "en": "So now after created and beforeMount, we reach mounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 148.41,
          "end": 150.76,
          "en": "So that in the end just means that now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.76,
          "end": 152.57,
          "en": "we see something on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.57,
          "end": 154.68,
          "en": "Now the Vue app was initialized",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.68,
          "end": 156.42000000000002,
          "en": "the template was compiled,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 156.42000000000002,
          "end": 158.68,
          "en": "Vue knows what to show on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 158.68,
          "end": 162.873,
          "en": "And it handed those instructions off to the browser,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 162.873,
          "end": 167.45,
          "en": "so that the browser really adds all the HTML elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 167.45,
          "end": 172.123,
          "en": "with all the content we need, as defined by our Vue app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.01,
          "end": 175.19,
          "en": "So now we have our mounted Vue app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.19,
          "end": 177.91,
          "en": "our Mountain Vue Instance.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 177.91,
          "end": 181.87,
          "en": "Now of course, in most Vue apps data changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.87,
          "end": 183.37,
          "en": "at some point of time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.37,
          "end": 186.67,
          "en": "And that then triggers a new life cycle.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 186.67,
          "end": 189.91,
          "en": "Now we reach the beforeUpdate hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 189.91,
          "end": 193.44,
          "en": "and there after the updated hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 193.44,
          "end": 196.12,
          "en": "This is a bit like beforeCreate and created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.12,
          "end": 199.42000000000002,
          "en": "BeforeUpdate is reached before the update",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.42000000000002,
          "end": 204.3,
          "en": "has been fully processed internally by Vue in its app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 204.3,
          "end": 208.03300000000002,
          "en": "updated is reached, once that has been processed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 209.18,
          "end": 212.41,
          "en": "This by the way, also means that at this point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 212.41,
          "end": 215.3,
          "en": "the update is visible on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 215.3,
          "end": 217.51,
          "en": "So we don't reach mounted again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 217.51,
          "end": 220.84,
          "en": "because the template was never unmounted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 220.84,
          "end": 222.65,
          "en": "so it always was visible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.65,
          "end": 226.22,
          "en": "After updated, the changes just have been processed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 226.22,
          "end": 228.45,
          "en": "and have been rendered to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.45,
          "end": 231.023,
          "en": "Whereas in beforeUpdate, they haven't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.22,
          "end": 235.03,
          "en": "Now sometimes, an instance can also be unmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 235.03,
          "end": 238.21,
          "en": "A Vue app can be unmounted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.21,
          "end": 241.16,
          "en": "We haven't had this scenario yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.16,
          "end": 244.36,
          "en": "it will become more important later, as you will see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.36,
          "end": 245.74,
          "en": "But I can also show you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 245.74,
          "end": 248.9,
          "en": "how we could unmount an app in the next lecture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 248.9,
          "end": 252.7,
          "en": "When an app is unmounted all its content is removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 252.7,
          "end": 255.25,
          "en": "from the screen and the app is dead.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 255.25,
          "end": 257.65,
          "en": "And we have two lifecycle hooks here as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 257.65,
          "end": 260.53,
          "en": "BeforeUnmount, which runs right before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 260.53,
          "end": 262.27,
          "en": "it's about to be removed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 262.27,
          "end": 265.63,
          "en": "and unmounted, which runs after it has been removed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 265.63,
          "end": 268.3,
          "en": "You can for example, use these hooks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 268.3,
          "end": 271.48,
          "en": "to execute any cleanup code you might wanna do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 271.48,
          "end": 274.24,
          "en": "send a HTTP request to your server",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 274.24,
          "end": 276.74,
          "en": "to keep track of that app being unmounted",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 276.74,
          "end": 279.21,
          "en": "or whatever you need to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 279.21,
          "end": 281.73,
          "en": "Now let's see all those hooks in action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 281.73,
          "end": 284.303,
          "en": "to make it a bit clearer how they work.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
